        "original_id": "a719d2a3-0edc-595d-bcd6-85da6a0fb4f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Horton Foote, David Foster Wallace, Thomas C. Ryan, K.B. Gilden, Katya Gilden, Bert Gilden\n- Works: To Kill a Mockingbird, Tender Mercies, Hurry Sundown, Hurry Sundown novel\n- Topics: American writing, screenwriting, live television dramas, Golden Age of Television\n\nFacts:\n- Albert Horton Foote Jr. was born on March 14, 1916, and was an American playwright and screenwriter.\n- Horton Foote was known for writing the screenplays for the 1962 film To Kill a Mockingbird and the 1983 film Tender Mercies.\n- Horton Foote was also notable for his live television dramas during the Golden Age of Television.\n- David Foster Wallace was born on February 21, 1962, and was an American writer and university instructor of English and creative writing.\n- The screenplay for Hurry Sundown was written by Horton Foote and Thomas C. Ryan.\n- The screenplay for Hurry Sundown was based on the 1965 novel of the same title.\n- K.B. Gilden was the pseudonym of the married couple Katya Gilden and Bert Gilden.\n- David Foster Wallace died on September 12, 2008.\n- Horton Foote died on March 4, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
